{"id": "5455e096-4dcb-43dc-93a1-db6bf60003b9", "role": "assistant", "block_type": "thinking", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "This points to permissions as the root cause: no bucket policy, SSE-S3 so no KMS involved, and the error message indicates an implicit deny from missing identity-based policy rather than an explicit SCP block. No health event is open, and both jobs show COMPLETE status despite failing on their single scanned document — which explains why it "fails every time." I also couldn't list the bucket, suggesting the agent role lacks the necessary s3:ListBucket permission.

The inline policy has s3:ListBucket but not s3:GetObject, so that's the actual gap to fix; the vector store permission itself looks fine. This connects to two findings — one around missing GetObject access, and another around the knowledge base never successfully indexing any documents, since no COMPLETE job has ever reported indexed documents greater than zero, meaning retrieval returns nothing despite the misleading COMPLETE status label. I should scope out what I haven't verified, like SCPs, CloudTrail, and vector store encryption, and make sure to mask the account ID and role ARN when citing findings.

